     {
      "id": "rain_light_0p5mmh_taylor",
      "description": "WETTING BRANCH, light rain at the fire step. Reference: the EarthSciML fuel-moisture kernel driver data/eqwefic/fire_build/fmc_rain/fmc_rain_driver.F90, which calls fmc_wrffire_t%Advance_moisture_classes of the instrumented fork (ctessum-claude/fire_behavior @ 8d519c6, default real32) directly on an 8-cell strip whose accumulated rain spans the 0.05 mm/h threshold; this is cell 4 of call 1 (dump run_fmc_rain/esm_dump_fmc_1.json), rain_int = 0.5 mm/h over dt_moisture = 0.5 s. Why it exists: both reference RUNS this repo has -- test7 and the coupled Last Chance Gulch case -- are rain-free (fire_rain is identically 0 for the whole 12 h fire), so physics/fmc_wrffire_mod.F90:338-345 was transcribed but never executed by any test. In this regime r = rain_int - 0.05 = 0.45 > 0, so the equilibrium bracket collapses to emc_d = emc_w = saturation_moisture + deltas = 2.5 (every class is driven towards 250 % moisture regardless of where it starts) and rlag becomes the wetting lag scaled by 1 - exp(-r/8) = 0.0547. change = dt rlag is still far below TOL, so the update takes the second-order Taylor branch. The 2 m forcing is cell (18,64) of test7 step 20 so the drying-branch control (no_rain_600s_exponential) is directly comparable. real32: rel 1e-5.",
      "expression_template_imports": [{"ref": "./tests/rain_state_fmc005_cat2_inputs.esm"}],
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "rain": 6.944444612599909e-05,
